Id: sctl004w
Severity: WARN
Category: kernel
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set kern.elf32.aslr.enable=1 and kern.elf64.aslr.enable=1 in /etc/sysctl.conf.
References: sysctl.conf(5); sysctl(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 10.5; NIST CM-6, SI-16; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

Address space layout randomisation is off for the binaries named
(32-bit, 64-bit, or both): their code and libraries load at the same
addresses every time, so whoever corrupts one's memory knows where
everything is. FreeBSD randomises both unless told otherwise:
  # sysctl -w kern.elf64.aslr.enable=1
and keep both keys in /etc/sysctl.conf.
